{"k": "general:95a258b7d9a43980dad73c8b878e2cdd7c643254420faa7313237c9ff2139aaf", "v": {"text": "To find how long it takes to climb 3000 meters at a rate of **7.645 m/s**, we can use the formula:\n\n$$\n\\text{Time} = \\frac{\\text{Distance}}{\\text{Rate of climb}}\n$$\n\n### Given:\n- Distance = 3000 m  \n- Rate of climb = 7.645 m/s\n\n### Step-by-step:\n$$\n\\text{Time} = \\frac{3000}{7.645} \\approx 392.24 \\text{ seconds}\n$$\n\nNow convert seconds to minutes:\n\n$$\n\\text{Time} = \\frac{392.24}{60} \\approx 6.54 \\text{ minutes}\n$$\n\n### \u2705 Final Answer:\n**6.54 minutes** (approximately)", "tokens": 185}}
