{"k": "general:00de78d75686f336fd438754a3df028f9be38cc49f46742df0ca142e8d905068", "v": {"text": "To find how far the aircraft can fly, we need to know:\n\n1. **Endurance (time it can fly)**:  \n   From the first question, we know the aircraft carries 4000 kg of fuel and burns 800 kg per hour.  \n   So, **endurance = 4000 kg \u00f7 800 kg/hour = 5 hours**.\n\n2. **Speed**: 220 m/s\n\n---\n\n### Step 1: Convert speed to km/h  \nSince 1 m/s = 3.6 km/h,  \n$$\n220 \\, \\text{m/s} \\times 3.6 = 792 \\, \\text{km/h}\n$$\n\n---\n\n### Step 2: Calculate distance  \n$$\n\\text{Distance} = \\text{Speed} \\times \\text{Time} = 792 \\, \\text{km/h} \\times 5 \\, \\text{hours} = 3960 \\, \\text{km}\n$$\n\n---\n\n### \u2705 Final Answer: **3960 kilometers**", "tokens": 240}}
