{"k": "general:8e4871d49d216496392b54cf30a56dbf09e04ccb6566e29b801d566c605902c6", "v": {"text": "To find the **exhaust velocity** of the rocket engine, we can use the relationship between **specific impulse (Isp)**, **exhaust velocity (ve)**, and **standard gravity (g\u2080)**:\n\n$$\nv_e = I_{sp} \\cdot g_0\n$$\n\n### Given:\n- Specific impulse, $ I_{sp} = 450 \\, \\text{s} $\n- Standard gravity, $ g_0 = 9.81 \\, \\text{m/s}^2 $\n\n### Calculation:\n$$\nv_e = 450 \\times 9.81 = 4414.5 \\, \\text{m/s}\n$$\n\n### \u2705 Final Answer:\n$$\n\\boxed{4414.5 \\, \\text{m/s}}\n$$", "tokens": 174}}
{"k": "general:30418872f1b2c98823e17b71107e75d09e05e224a6bed19174c93a41af4ce276", "v": {"text": "To calculate the **aspect ratio** of a wing, you use the formula:\n\n$$\n\\text{Aspect Ratio} = \\frac{\\text{Span}^2}{\\text{Wing Area}}\n$$\n\n### Given:\n- **Span** = 36 m  \n- **Wing Area** = 100 m\u00b2\n\n### Calculation:\n$$\n\\text{Aspect Ratio} = \\frac{36^2}{100} = \\frac{1296}{100} = 12.96\n$$\n\n### Final Answer:\n$$\n\\boxed{12.96}\n$$", "tokens": 135}}
{"k": "general:6aaf81914a5fdf2064acf7ee8891b2cc1d3f37e5abc26ed57581f845771afcb4", "v": {"text": "To find the **aspect ratio** of a wing, we use the formula:\n\n$$\n\\text{Aspect Ratio} = \\frac{\\text{Span}^2}{\\text{Wing Area}}\n$$\n\n### Given:\n- **Span** = 30 m  \n- **Wing Area** = 120 m\u00b2\n\n### Calculation:\n$$\n\\text{Aspect Ratio} = \\frac{30^2}{120} = \\frac{900}{120} = 7.5\n$$\n\n### Final Answer:\n$$\n\\boxed{7.5}\n$$\n\nSo, the aspect ratio is **7.5**.", "tokens": 143}}
{"k": "general:f0d3b54e5d3a9201630aee6c073cc928a2bd4717ab45a9a864ac16918487a8d5", "v": {"text": "To find the **mean chord** of a wing, we use the formula:\n\n$$\n\\text{Mean Chord} = \\frac{\\text{Wing Area}}{\\text{Wing Span}}\n$$\n\n### Given:\n- Wing span = 30 m  \n- Wing area = 100 m\u00b2  \n\n### Calculation:\n$$\n\\text{Mean Chord} = \\frac{100}{30} = \\frac{10}{3} \\approx 3.33 \\text{ m}\n$$\n\n### \u2705 Final Answer:\n$$\n\\boxed{3.33 \\text{ m}}\n$$", "tokens": 135}}
